{"area": "writing", "family": "email", "id": "writing-dev-001", "judged": {"rubric": "writing/1"}, "provenance": {"author": "neuroshard general-eval development authoring", "source": "fresh", "written": "2026-10-30"}, "scoring": {"constraints": [{"kind": "paragraphs", "n": 3}, {"kind": "include", "word": "tap"}, {"kind": "max_words", "n": 119}], "kind": "constraints"}, "split": "development", "turns": [{"user": "Write the body of a short email to my landlord asking when the broken kitchen tap will be repaired, with no greeting line and no sign-off. Use exactly three paragraphs, mention the word \"tap\", and keep it under 120 words."}]}
{"area": "writing", "family": "summary", "id": "writing-dev-002", "judged": {"rubric": "writing/1"}, "provenance": {"author": "neuroshard general-eval development authoring", "source": "fresh", "written": "2026-10-30"}, "scoring": {"constraints": [{"kind": "max_words", "n": 40}, {"kind": "include_all", "words": ["roof", "March"]}], "kind": "constraints"}, "split": "development", "turns": [{"user": "Summarise this notice in at most 40 words, and make sure the words \"roof\" and \"March\" appear:\n\nOur town library will close its east wing from 3 to 21 March so that the roof can be replaced. During the closure the children's section moves to the community hall on Bridge Street, and returns can be made at the front desk as usual. Evening opening on Thursdays is suspended until the work is finished. The library thanks residents for their patience and expects the new roof to cut heating costs by a quarter."}]}
{"area": "writing", "family": "summary", "id": "writing-dev-003", "judged": {"rubric": "writing/1"}, "provenance": {"author": "neuroshard general-eval development authoring", "source": "fresh", "written": "2026-10-30"}, "scoring": {"constraints": [{"kind": "bullets", "n": 3}], "kind": "constraints"}, "split": "development", "turns": [{"user": "Give me three bullet points, and nothing else, with the practical facts a parent needs from this notice:\n\nOur town library will close its east wing from 3 to 21 March so that the roof can be replaced. During the closure the children's section moves to the community hall on Bridge Street, and returns can be made at the front desk as usual. Evening opening on Thursdays is suspended until the work is finished. The library thanks residents for their patience and expects the new roof to cut heating costs by a quarter."}]}
